Task #940: Surface merge-conflict recovery events on the operator dashboard

Adds operator-visible surfacing for the LC4 dev-builder
`merge_conflict_recovery` audit envelopes that the recovery handler
stamps onto `system.execution_tasks.payload` when the loop auto-replans
on a hard drift overlap.

Changes
- Extended `createMergeConflictAuditHandler` in
  `supabase/functions/_shared/execution/builders/merge-conflict-recovery.ts`
  to include a deduplicated `files: string[]` field in the audit entry,
  enabling per-file aggregation downstream.
- New repository
  `src/repositories/merge-conflict-recovery.repository.ts`:
  - `fetchMergeConflictRecoveryEvents` now keyset-paginates over
    `system.execution_tasks` (PAGE_SIZE 500, MAX_PAGES 100) so 14-day
    aggregates do not silently undercount under load. Replaces the
    earlier 200-row hard cap.
  - Pure `projectMergeConflictRecoverySummary` produces per-day buckets,
    top-5 files, totals, and affected task count.
- New page
  `src/pages/admin/AdminMergeConflictRecoveryPage.tsx`:
  - Metrics, 14-day bar chart, top-5 conflicting paths, recent events
    list.
  - Deep linking is shareable: clicking an event writes
    `?taskId=<id>` to the URL; the same URL pre-opens the drawer on
    load. The drawer fetches the affected `system.execution_tasks`
    row by id (`dashboardRepo.fetchExecutionTaskById`).
  - "Open in Command & Control" forwards the task id as
    `/admin/command-control?tab=live-tasks&taskId=<id>`.
- `CommandControlDashboard` honors `?tab=` to land on the live-tasks
  tab.
- `ExecutionTaskPanel` reads `?taskId=` from the URL: pulls that row
  by id (independent of the active status filter), pins it to the top
  of the list, and scroll-highlights it with a ring — completing the
  shareable deep link from the recovery dashboard into the live
  builder task row.
- `AdminOpsDashboardPage` (the operator dashboard) embeds a
  `MergeConflictRecoveryWidget` panel that shows the 14-day event
  count, affected task count, and top file, and links to the full
  detail page.
- Wired into the route registry and `AdminRoutes` at
  `/admin/merge-conflict-recovery`.

Code-review iterations addressed
1. First review: original `?taskId=` link did not resolve in any
   downstream surface. Fixed with an in-page drawer.
2. Second review:
   - Deep link is now URL-driven (shareable / bookmarkable) and
     forwards into Command & Control, which pins/highlights the row.
   - Surfacing on the operator dashboard added as a panel widget on
     `AdminOpsDashboardPage`.
   - Removed the 200-row cap; replaced with paginated keyset scan.

Validation
- LSP diagnostics clean across the project.
- `npx vitest run src/__tests__/lc4-merge-conflict-recovery.test.ts`:
  42/42 pass (handler audit + new projection tests).

No deviations from the task brief.

